  "note": "RFC 7911 Section 2: \"A BGP speaker that re-advertises a route MUST generate its own Path Identifier to be associated with the re-advertised route.\" Every current tagged cover was read. The core collision/stability units and generation units assert distinct source paths for one prefix, stable replacement despite attribute changes, exact inverse withdrawals, unframed sources, legal received and locally assigned zero/maximum values, per-neighbor stability and collision avoidance at wrap. TestForwardPathIDMPGeneration checks exact native prefix/identifier pairs on raw MP, cross-context and unframed-source rails, including reversed-order replacement and withdrawal; TestPathIDKeyFollowsWhatTheSourceFramed keeps a sibling prefix stable after another is retired. All four churn units assert recipient-visible identities through relay, cache acknowledgement and final writes, including rebuilt frames and a pair withdrawn and re-announced in one UPDATE. Their bodies are unchanged; newSyncOrderDest now publishes the supplied framing through real capability negotiation. The functional replay carrier compares exact live/replayed daemon bytes; its pinned first local identifier zero is a fixture fact, not an RFC allocator requirement. The foreign checker requires FRR to retain both source origins under different identifiers and retain each pairing after reconnect; its predicates were read, but no foreign run is claimed here. The changed AS-zero writer preserves original ingress identity while projecting held routes into compliant withdrawals, with its inspected projection boundaries added to code fingerprints. Memory-release assertions are Ze contracts, and numeric inequality from a received identifier is not itself an RFC obligation. Native renewal of the four churn records remains a main-thread step, not an observation made by this source audit.",
